Since right pointer is used for two purposes, the boolean variable rightThread is used to indicate whether right pointer points to right child or inorder successor. Similarly, we can add leftThread for a double threaded binary tree.Inorder Traversal using Threads Following is code for inorder traversal in a threaded binary tree.
            C++

    // Utility function to find leftmost node in a tree rooted with n
Node* leftMost(Node* n){
    if (n == NULL)
        return NULL;

    while (n->left != NULL)
        n = n->left;

    return n;
}

// CPP code to do inorder traversal in a threaded binary tree
void inOrder(Node* root){
    Node* cur = leftMost(root);
    while (cur != NULL) {
        cout<<cur->data<<" ";

        // If this node is a thread node, then go to
        // inorder successor
        if (cur->rightThread)
            cur = cur->right;
        else // Else go to the leftmost child in right
             // subtree
            cur = leftmost(cur->right);
    }
}

